    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000123083,
      "SummaryText": "Church and Dwight Cloverleaf York Regional Distribution Center \n\nA risk management plan has been implemented at the Cloverleaf York facility for the prevention of accidental releases of hazardous materials. The facility is located at 250 Cloverleaf Road, York, PA 17406 in York County. The facility is a storage and distribution warehouse for consumer products, such as dry shampoo and deodorants, packaged in aerosol cans for retail sale. The products are manufactured at a different location by Church and Dwight company. The operator of the facility is DHL Supply Chain, a subsidiary of Deutsch Post Ag, Bonn, Germany. \n\nThe propellant used in the aerosol products contains several components that are classified as flammable materials. The maximum projected quantities of aerosol products stored in the warehouse and product propellants weights were used to estimate maximum quantities of RMP regulated chemicals in the warehouse storage process.\n\nThe worst case scenario performed, based on the EPA's ecomp program, indicates that the distance to the 1 psi overpressure endpoint will not extend beyond the warehouse property. No offsite receptors are impacted. Since this is a new building for the operation, no prior accidents have occurred at the facility.\n\nThe site has a comprehensive Environmental, Health, and Safety program including corporate policies and procedures, site specific work instructions, formal employee training, annual emergency drills, regular inspections, emergency supplies and internal assessments. Emergency response activities at the facility are coordinated with the York County LEPC and the local fire department."
    }
  ]
